course: dictionary
lesson: 3487
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word fan is a good example. Read the words around it: they are its context, and they tell you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «Danylo tells history like a football fan» uses fan for a person who loves a team very much. The clues are football and history. In «the fan on after a steamy bath» the clues are steamy and bath, so fan means a machine that moves air.
explain: Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. Try "a machine that moves air" in the bathroom sentence: it fits. Try "a person who loves a team" there: it does not. Then you know which meaning is right.
fact: Fan can be a noun (a fan, fans) or a verb (fan, fans, fanned, fanning).
fact: A fan is a person who likes a sport, team, singer, book or hobby very much.
fact: A fan is a machine with spinning blades that moves air to cool you down.
fact: A fan does not make the air colder; it moves air over your skin so sweat dries faster and you feel cooler.
fact: To fan means to move air towards something, or to spread out in a fan shape: fan out.
exercise: «Danylo, a boy in the class, tells history like a football fan.» What does fan mean here? | A machine with spinning blades | A flat folding object for waving | *A person who loves a team very much | To spread out in a shape
exercise: «...the fan on after a steamy bath.» What is the fan in this sentence? | To spread out | *A machine that moves air | A person who loves a singer | A flat object you wave in front of your face
exercise: Mia is hot, so she waves a fan in front of her face. What is the fan? | *A flat folding object you wave to cool yourself | A machine with spinning blades on a ceiling | A team supporter | To move air towards something
test: «Engineers have copied the bumps for fan and turbine blades.» Here fan means? | To spread out in a shape | A folding object you wave | A person who loves whales | *A machine part with spinning blades that moves air
test: Ben says, "The campers fanned out across the field to search for the lost ball." What does fanned out mean? | Switched off a machine | Waved a folding object | *Spread out in a fan shape | Cheered for a team
exam: «Fans have bodies as well as players: three hours in July sun can bring on heat exhaustion.» In this sentence fans means? | A machine that moves air | A flat folding object | *People who love a sport very much | To move air towards something
